From 5423f4ec9c35be66592c61cb2da2ccd7ca5e7337 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:33:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/22] can: isotp: drop frames without N_PCI

isotp_rcv() reads the address extension and the N_PCI without checking
the CAN frame data length. So frames with CAN_DL < ae + N_PCI_SZ are
processed with the data bytes beyond CAN_DL, e.g. as SF, CF or FC.

As the data of the CAN frame structure is always present, the reads stay
within the skb. But with the zero-filled data from CAN drivers a frame
with CAN_DL 0 was processed as SF with SF_DL 0, which terminated an
ongoing reception.

Drop these frames as they are no valid N_PDUs. As only invalid frames
are affected, there is no Fixes tag.

Signed-off-by: Oliver Hartkopp <socketcan@hartkopp.net>
---
 net/can/isotp.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/can/isotp.c b/net/can/isotp.c
index b237b1f..798c1b4 100644
--- a/net/can/isotp.c
+++ b/net/can/isotp.c
@@ -775,6 +775,10 @@ static void isotp_rcv(struct sk_buff *skb, void *data)
 
 	cf = (struct canfd_frame *)skb->data;
 
+	/* frames without N_PCI (and AE) are no N_PDUs */
+	if (cf->len < ae + N_PCI_SZ)
+		return;
+
 	/* if enabled: check reception of my configured extended address */
 	if (ae && cf->data[0] != so->opt.rx_ext_address)
 		return;
